# Copy to `.env.local` (gitignored) and fill in REAL values. NEVER commit real
# secrets.
#
# The filename matters: the local real stack reads repo-root `.env.local`, not
# `.env`. Both `pnpm dev` and `pnpm db:migrate` load it through
# services/local-learner-api/src/env-file.ts, so a file named `.env` leaves them
# reporting `DATABASE_URL is not set`. See docs/runbooks/local-real-stack.md.
#
# First run: `pnpm install`, create this file and apps/learner-web/.env.local,
# `pnpm db:migrate`, `pnpm dev` — then accept the self-signed certificate once at
# https://localhost:5173.
#
# `pnpm dev:offline` needs nothing from this file. It runs the in-process dev
# authority over in-memory storage with a dev auth stand-in — no database and no
# Supabase. It does still need apps/learner-web/.env.local, which carries the
# VITE_AUTHORITY_BASE_URL the client requires in either mode.

# Postgres connection for the data layer (@mcat/persistence-postgres →
# createDatabasePoolFromEnv). Same variable for local Postgres, Supabase, or Aurora.
#
# LEFT EMPTY ON PURPOSE: it carries the database password, so it is the one value
# that cannot live in a tracked file. Ask a teammate for the shared dev string.
#
# It must be the Supabase TRANSACTION POOLER on port 6543:
#   postgresql://postgres.<ref>:<password>@aws-1-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres
# The session pooler (port 5432 on the same host) does not answer for this
# project, and the direct host (db.<ref>.supabase.co) is IPv6-only, which is why
# it appears to hang. `pnpm db:migrate` detects the transaction pooler and skips
# the session-scoped migration advisory lock, printing that it did.
DATABASE_URL=

# TLS mode:
#   require    → verify the server certificate (default; use for AWS RDS/Aurora)
#   no-verify  → TLS without cert verification (managed Postgres such as Supabase)
#   disable    → no TLS (local Postgres only)
DATABASE_SSL=no-verify

# Which Supabase project's signing keys the local learner API verifies tokens
# against. Public — it is the subdomain of the project URL. Must name the SAME
# project as VITE_SUPABASE_URL in apps/learner-web/.env.local, or every sign-in
# fails issuer verification.
SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF=iimihnwlqbsjzemvwupl

# ORIGIN_VERIFICATION_SECRET and RATE_LIMIT_PEPPER are NOT listed here on
# purpose: `pnpm dev` generates both per-machine on first run, appends them to
# `.env.local`, and says so. They are written to the file rather than held in
# memory because the Vite proxy must send the same origin-verification secret
# this process expects.
#
# So do not set them by hand and do not copy them from a teammate's machine.
# Each machine generates its own pair, the proxy and the local API must read the
# SAME pair from the same file, and a mismatch makes every `/v1` call return 403.
